    band: 'inland',
    title: 'Turf Cleaning in Red Hill, SC | TIMELESS',
    description: `Turf cleaning in Red Hill: the high, dry ground next to Coastal Carolina University's athletic campus. Call ${brand.phone}.`,
    h1: 'Turf cleaning in Red Hill',
    intro: `Red Hill sits on a sand ridge at 36 feet of elevation, the highest and best-drained ground anywhere in our service area, a 1990s-and-2000s commuter belt of covenant-governed subdivisions along US 501 and SC 544. There's no swamp here and no salt air twelve miles inland; what actually stresses turf on these open, treeless lots is heat and UV under a Carolina summer sun. Coastal Carolina University's athletic campus sits right at the community's edge, Brooks Stadium's turf installed in 2015 and now at the age synthetic fields get replaced. Homeowners here answer to an architectural review committee before they change anything visible from the street, and cleaning is one of the few things on the property that doesn't need its approval.`,
    question: 'Who cleans artificial turf in Red Hill?',
    answer: `TIMELESS Turf Restoration cleans and restores artificial turf and backyard putting greens across Red Hill, along the US 501 and SC 544 corridor near Coastal Carolina University. Owner-operated by Brian, 13 years in turf. Essential Clean from $199, Premium Restoration from $299, priced by square foot; no HOA approval needed for cleaning.`,
    image: { src: '/assets/img/practice-nets-and-goals-on-turf.jpg', alt: 'Practice nets and goals on artificial turf' },
    blocks: [
      { h2: 'The high ground', html: `<p>At 36 feet of elevation on a real sand ridge above the Waccamaw floodplain, Red Hill has the best natural drainage in our whole service area, upland Coastal Plain sand rather than the flatwoods that sit wet everywhere else on the Strand. What stresses turf here instead is heat and ultraviolet exposure: open, largely treeless 501-corridor lots that take a full South Carolina summer sun with nothing shading them, on subgrade that was scraped and compacted during the 1990s and 2000s build-out. The fix isn't drainage work, it's a clean that gets the heat-baked dust and pollen out of the infill before it packs down further. <a href="/services/artificial-turf-cleaning/">Artificial turf cleaning</a>.</p>` },
      { h2: 'The committee, not the county', html: `<p>Red Hill is unincorporated, so there's no municipal building department reviewing what you do to your yard, but the 1990s master-planned subdivisions that make up most of the housing here run their own architectural review committees, and that's the real gate. Under South Carolina's Homeowners Association Act, a covenant has to be recorded with the Horry County Register of Deeds, and re-recorded every January, to be enforceable at all. A turf cleaning changes nothing an ARC reviews; it's a repair or a visible infill change that sometimes needs a submittal, and we'll flag it if yours does.</p>` },
      { h2: 'Brooks Stadium is ten years old', html: `<p>Coastal Carolina University's athletics campus sits right at Red Hill's edge, and Brooks Stadium has carried its teal synthetic surface since 2015, which puts it near the end of a typical field's service life. Springs Brooks Stadium next door is still natural grass. The backyard greens in the neighborhoods around the Wizard, the Witch and Man O'War, all a short drive down 501, get the same seasonal restoration a stadium field does on a smaller scale: cleared, top-dressed, brushed and rolled. <a href="/services/putting-green-restoration/">Putting green restoration</a>.</p>` },
      { h2: 'No salt, no swamp, just pollen', html: `<p>Twelve to thirteen miles from the ocean, Red Hill turf has no salt-spray corrosion to worry about, and the western edge toward the Waccamaw floodplain is the exception rather than the rule for standing water. The one thing every yard here shares with the rest of the Strand is pine pollen every March, and a late-May Premium Restoration, after the pollen has stopped, is the best-timed visit of the year.</p>` },
    ],
    communities: ['Red Hill Commons'],
    golf: ['The Wizard', 'The Witch', `Man O'War`, 'Wild Wing Golf Course', 'Legends Golf & Resort', 'The Hackler Course at CCU'],
    pets: ['Carolina Forest Veterinary Hospital (nearby)'],
    faq: [
      { q: 'Does turf cleaning need HOA approval in Red Hill?', a: `No. Cleaning changes nothing an architectural review committee looks at. A repair or a front-yard infill change occasionally does, and we'll say so before we start.` },
      { q: 'Is heat the main problem for Red Hill turf, not water?', a: 'Usually, yes. The ground here is the best-drained in our service area. What ages turf on these open 501-corridor lots is sun and UV, plus pine pollen every spring, not standing water.' },
    ],
